<ContentLayout title="Acodot 9-in-1 USB-C Hub vs Anker 553 8-in-1: Which Laptop Hub Should You Buy? | StackGeist" description="Both are popular USB-C hubs. Acodot is cheaper with more single-port variety. Anker 553 has dual HDMI and better warranty support. Here is the honest comparison." active="gear">
  <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">StackGeist</a> / <a href="/gear">Gear</a> / <a href="/gear/budget-tech">Budget tech</a> / <a href="/gear/budget-tech/compare">Compare</a> / Acodot vs Anker 553</p>
  <p class="page-kicker">Head to head</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Acodot 9-in-1 vs Anker 553 8-in-1 USB-C Hub</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">Both hubs solve the same problem: modern laptops don't have enough ports. The Acodot is cheaper and includes SD + microSD + audio jack. The Anker 553 gives up card readers to add a second HDMI output. Pick based on whether you need two external monitors or just more everyday ports.</p>

  <section class="content-section">
    <table class="cmp">
      <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Acodot 9-in-1 USB-C Hub</th><th>Anker 553 8-in-1 USB-C Hub</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><tr><td>Price</td><td>$20-25</td><td>$45-55</td></tr>
<tr><td>HDMI outputs</td><td>1 (4K30 / 1080p60)</td><td>2 (each 4K30 / 1080p60)</td></tr>
<tr><td>USB-A ports</td><td>3 x USB 3.0</td><td>2 x USB 3.0</td></tr>
<tr><td>USB-C data port</td><td>1 x 5 Gbps</td><td>1 x 5 Gbps</td></tr>
<tr><td>SD / microSD readers</td><td>Both, UHS-I</td><td>None</td></tr>
<tr><td>3.5mm audio</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gigabit Ethernet</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td>PD pass-through max</td><td>~87W to laptop (100W input)</td><td>~85W to laptop (100W input)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Warranty</td><td>12-18 months</td><td>18 months + Anker support</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">When Acodot 9-in-1 USB-C Hub wins</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Pick Acodot 9-in-1 USB-C Hub if...</h2>
    <p>You need SD or microSD card readers. Photographers, drone pilots, dash-cam users all pull cards multiple times a week. The Acodot's card readers are UHS-I capable (up to 104 MB/s) — not the fastest, but built in and always at hand.</p><p>You need a 3.5mm audio jack because your laptop doesn't have one (Framework, some Dell XPS models). The Acodot includes it as a real audio port.</p><p>You want the cheapest way to get one external monitor plus USB-A ports plus card readers. Under $25 for the full loadout.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">When Anker 553 8-in-1 USB-C Hub wins</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Pick Anker 553 8-in-1 USB-C Hub if...</h2>
    <p>You run two external monitors from a single-port laptop. Dual HDMI on one hub is the reason the Anker 553 costs twice as much. Note: on M-series Macs (non-Pro), both HDMI outputs mirror, not extend — this is a macOS limitation, not the hub's.</p><p>You want Gigabit Ethernet. Office Wi-Fi is congested; wired connection is faster and lower latency. The Acodot doesn't have Ethernet.</p><p>You want Anker's warranty and support process. Their return / replacement handling is better than Acodot's average response time.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">The verdict</p>
    <p>Two external monitors: Anker 553. Card readers and 3.5mm audio: Acodot. If you don't need either, Acodot at half the price is the correct default.</p><p>Neither is a Thunderbolt dock replacement. If you need 4K60, 10 Gbps data, or eGPU support, you need a real Thunderbolt dock at $250+.</p>
  </section>

